@startuml
' Data-flow diagram with trust boundaries (dashed = boundary crossing).
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #333333
  FontColor #10223A
}

package "Browser origin (host-controlled)" #EAF2FB {
  rectangle "Host web application\n(trusted by itself)" as host #4F86C6
  rectangle "<Editor> + library\n(runs with host privileges)" as editor #4F86C6
  rectangle "DataScript DB\n(in-memory, no persistence)" as db #F5E0C3
}

package "Same-origin sandbox" #F1EAF7 {
  rectangle "Tree-Sitter core + grammar\n(WebAssembly)" as wasm #8E7CC3
  rectangle ".scm highlight/indent queries" as scm #8E7CC3
}

cloud "Language server\n(UNTRUSTED input)" as lsp #F8D7DA

host --> editor : props / ref / events
editor --> db : query() / getDb()\n(exposes DB to host)
editor ..> wasm : loads + executes\n(supply-chain trust)
editor ..> scm : loads + runs
editor <..> lsp : #B22222

note right of lsp #F8D7DA
  Boundary 1 (network): ws:// is
  UNAUTHENTICATED + PLAINTEXT by default.
  Treat every message (diagnostics, symbols,
  logs) as untrusted input.
end note

note bottom of wasm
  Boundary 2 (supply chain): grammar WASM and
  .scm queries are code that runs against input.
  data:/Blob URLs may embed them.
end note

note top of host
  Boundary 3 (host trust): getDb()/query() hand the
  host app full read access to the editor's DataScript DB.
end note
@enduml
